       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 4000 mg four times daily is 16,000 mg/day, which is 5 times the usual maximum daily dose. The maximum is 3,200 mg/day for prescription use, and 1,200 mg/day for over-the-counter use. A dose that high risks serious GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular and CNS toxicity. Because the dose looks like a possible typo, I'd like to confirm it with you first.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **400 mg PO four times daily** (1,600 mg/day), a common regimen\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day), a common regimen for inflammatory conditions\n- **600 mg PO four times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 4000 mg per dose, please confirm that and give me the clinical rationale. I'll add it to the order note."
