      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. 4000 mg per dose, four times daily, is 16,000 mg/day. That's well into the toxic range, and I know of no clinical indication for it. At that dose, serious harm is likely, including GI hemorrhage, acute kidney injury, metabolic acidosis, and CNS effects. Your patient's normal kidney and liver function wouldn't protect against that.\n\nYou can still get the order placed in a couple of ways:\n- **Enter a corrected dose.** Give me the dose you want, such as 400 mg or 800 mg, and I'll enter it right away.\n- **Use a different pathway.** If you have a protocol or rationale I'm missing, such as a research protocol or a unit conversion issue, you can enter it directly in the order system. Pharmacy would also need to review it.\n\nIf the goal is stronger analgesia or anti-inflammatory effect, I can help with other options, like scheduled ibuprofen at 800 mg three times daily, adding acetaminophen, or another agent."
      }
